<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charroux</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charroux is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> that grew around a Benedictine abbey founded in the late 8th century and renowned for its relics. A church council held there in 989 issued the first known decrees of the Peace of God. In the 10th century its lords, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boso-the-old">Boso the Old</a>, became counts of La <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a>.</p></div>
